    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15495" root="رسل" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَسْلَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A soft,</i> or <i>delicate condition</i> of life: you
say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُمْ فِى رَسْلَةٍ مِنَ العَيْشِ</span> <i>They are in a soft,</i>
or <i>delicate, condition of life.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
<i>Heaviness, sluggishness, laziness,</i> or <i>indolence:</i>
(M, K:) you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ فِيهِ رَسْلَةٌ</span> <i>A man in whom
is heaviness,</i> &amp;c. (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِسْلٌ</span>, first
sentence.

